# Agentic Schemas Marketplace — `marketplace.json` Schema
#
# This file documents the format of `marketplace.json`, which lists
# all schemas in this repository for discovery by AI coding agents.
# The format follows the Claude Code marketplace plugin discovery spec.

## File Extension
`.json` — standard JSON, stored at `<repo-root>/.agent-schemas/marketplace.json`.

## Structure

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://anthropic.com/claude-code/marketplace.schema.json",
  "name": "onlygpus-schemas",              // Marketplace identifier
  "description": "Agentic schemas for...",   // One-line description
  "owner": {
    "name": "Ricardo Arturo Cabral Mejía",  // Author name
    "url": "https://example.com"            // Optional URL
  },
  "plugins": [                               // List of schema entries
    {
      "name": "opa-docker-authz",            // Schema directory name
      "description": "Grants a...",          // From SCHEMA.md frontmatter
      "source": "./opa-docker-authz",        // Relative path to schema dir
      "category": "infrastructure",          // Classification tag
      "author": {
        "name": "Ricardo Arturo Cabral Mejía",
        "url": "https://agenticschemas.ai"
      },
      "keywords": ["docker", "opa", "tls"]  // Search keywords
    }
  ]
}
```

## Fields

| Field | Required | Type | Description |
|-------|----------|------|-------------|
| `$schema` | yes | string | Validation schema URL |
| `name` | yes | string | Marketplace identifier (`onlygpus-schemas`) |
| `description` | yes | string | Brief description of the repo |
| `owner.name` | yes | string | Author's full name |
| `owner.email` | no | string | Contact email |
| `owner.url` | no | string | Author website |
| `plugins[].name` | yes | string | Schema name (matches directory) |
| `plugins[].description` | yes | string | From SCHEMA.md `description:` frontmatter |
| `plugins[].source` | yes | string | Relative path to schema directory |
| `plugins[].category` | yes | string | `infrastructure`, `engineering`, `devops`, etc. |
| `plugins[].keywords` | no | string[] | Search keywords |
| `plugins[].author.name` | no | string | Per-schema author override |
| `plugins[].author.email` | no | string | Per-schema author email |
| `plugins[].author.url` | no | string | Per-schema author URL |

## Adding a New Schema

1. Create `schemas/<name>/SCHEMA.md` with `description:` in frontmatter.
2. Add an entry to `plugins[]` in marketplace.json.
3. Commit and push.

## See Also

- `SCHEMA.md` — the full schema document for a single capability
- `docs/schemas/.agent-schemas/marketplace.json` — the actual file